  summary: 'After this chapter you can derive the 2×2 matrix of any scaling, rotation, projection, reflection or shear from the images of the basis vectors, apply x′ = Tx by hand (including exact surds at 30°, 45°, 60°), compose transformations in the correct order, use the determinant as an area scale factor, and reproduce all of it in NumPy.',
