          '$\\mathbf{e}_2=(0,1)$ sits at angle $90^\\circ$. After rotation it is at angle $\\theta+90^\\circ$, i.e. $(\\cos(\\theta+90^\\circ),\\sin(\\theta+90^\\circ))=(-\\sin\\theta,\;\\cos\\theta)$. So **column 2 is $(-\\sin\\theta,\\cos\\theta)$**.',
